: ASM_ARCH=i386_nasm_gnu :
: BLOCK_TEST :
: RUN_ASM :

:/
Reduced from log.log failures 28, 258, 454, 459 and other signed remainders.
Expected: -17 % 5 == -2, exit 42.
The i386 modulo path also emits CQO before IDIV ECX. NASM rejects CQO in
32-bit mode; this test exercises remainder lowering separately from division.
/:
@[inline(never)]
function remainder489(i32 value, i32 divisor) -> i32 {
    return value % divisor;
}

start() {
    if remainder489(-17i32, 5i32) != -2i32; { exit 1; }
    exit 42;
}

:/ OUTPUT
@exit_code=42
/:
